trong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482713-inventing-lgbt-characters-as-suggestions-for-onyx-writer-team?p=1496159#post1496159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to ignore it. I think you're an interesting character.And I agree about the LGBT thing. I'd add more sex in there, honestly. Although I realize that may not be what everyone wants, I'm just obsessed with it. Even last night I spent the evening with a <a href=\"https://&amp;quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">https://joynights.org/best-sex-pillow/&amp;quot;]</a><span style=\"color:#696969\">joynights</span>[/URL]-pillow instead of going out with friends. I think I'm a nymphomaniac.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Although maybe not quite to that extent (I waited till I got back from going out to use the pillow \ud83d\ude0a). But I do think there should be more recognition of sexuality in RPGs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T06:09:47-07:00","id":1496189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482713-inventing-lgbt-characters-as-suggestions-for-onyx-writer-team#post1482713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This orphan thread is the product of an attention-disorder, which is getting sorted out. <br /> <br /> Please ignore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry. Got distracted lol. But seriously, this is a great idea for a thread. Don\u2019t sell yourself short.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T14:06:16-08:00","id":1496539,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cybergirl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482713-inventing-lgbt-characters-as-suggestions-for-onyx-writer-team?p=1496159#post1496159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't want to ignore it. I think you're an interesting character.And I agree about the LGBT thing. I'd add more sex in there, honestly. Although I realize that may not be what everyone wants, I'm just obsessed with it. Even last night I spent the evening with a <a href=\"https://joynights.org/best-sex-pillow/\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#696969\">joynights</span></a>-pillow instead of going out with friends. I think I'm a nymphomaniac.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a straight man. At one time, my tagline read, &quot;He/Him... I just Love Witches.&quot;. I changed it to emphasize my preference for conversation over formal debate. Afterward changing to add an easily accessible link to the house rules that I use in Mage the Ascension. The Ascension game I run for a group began as a one on one with my girlfriend who chose the setting and decided on Verbena as the Tradition her character would join. My profile picture was taken from the still-frame in a YouTube video of the song, &quot;Black Crown&quot;, by Flesh. I was listening to a lot witch-house at the time.<br /> <br /> There was a comment on a now-inactive thread about cancel culture <i>external</i> to the fanbase of these games. The comment gave me the impression, in the way it was worded, that there would be a cancel culture <i>internal</i> to the fanbase of the games that discouraged writers from writing LGBT characters, too many or with too much description. The intention of this thread was to create a space in which <i>anyone or everyone</i> could post ideas for the kind of character they would like to see as members of the fanbase. These could range from a single line to however many pages.<br /> <br /> I have reconsidered the part about &quot;as suggestions for Onyx Writers Team&quot; in regard to any ideas I have. On the other hand, I'm happy to discuss witches and girl-girl romance in some other space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":26467,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","user":"HorizonParty2021","date":". 11-12-2022, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T15:27:40-08:00","id":1496549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482713-inventing-lgbt-characters-as-suggestions-for-onyx-writer-team?p=1496539#post1496539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a straight male. At one time, my tagline read, &amp;quot;He/Him... I just Love Witches.&amp;quot;. I changed it to emphasize my preference for conversation over formal debate. Afterward changing to add an easily accessible link to the house rules that I use in Mage the Ascension. The Ascension game I run for a group began as a one on one with my girlfriend who chose the setting and decided on Verbena as the Tradition her character would join. My profile picture was taken from the still-frame in a YouTube video of the song, &amp;quot;Black Crown&amp;quot;, by Flesh. I was listening to a lot witch-house at the time.<br /> <br /> There was a comment on a now-inactive thread about cancel culture <i>external</i> to the fanbase of these games. The comment gave me the impression, in the way it was worded, that there would be a cancel culture <i>internal</i> to the fanbase of the games that discouraged writers from writing LGBT characters, too many or with too much description. The intention of this thread was to create a space in which <i>anyone or everyone</i> could post ideas for the kind of character they would like to see as members of the fanbase. These could range from a single line to however many pages.<br /> <br /> I have reconsidered the part about &amp;quot;as suggestions for Onyx Writers Team&amp;quot; in regard to any ideas I have. On the other hand, I'm happy to discuss witches and girl-girl romance in some other space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Girl-girl romance (and LGBTQ+ romance in general) is actually a big part of Wicca, and I know a number of Wiccans who play WoD (and at least one who plays Trinity Continuum).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-08T18:34:25-08:00","id":1496565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482713-inventing-lgbt-characters-as-suggestions-for-onyx-writer-team?p=1496549#post1496549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Girl-girl romance (and LGBTQ+ romance in general) is actually a big part of Wicca, and I know a number of Wiccans who play WoD (and at least one who plays Trinity Continuum).</div> </div> </div> </div>My first serious girlfriend already had a girlfriend, both becoming frequent guests at my mother's place. &quot;We're playing Vampire.&quot;, I would say on our way up the stairs. I have not had any experience of that kind since, didn't pursue such and rarely speak of it, since it was habitual not to in a community whose views were unsupportive of how we felt, their own families included. One was an Atheist with a purely scientific worldview, the other a nominal Christian.<br /> <br /> Completely unconnected and years later, I was at a bus stop with a group of friends on a hot, humid day. A woman who I knew to be a practitioner of Wicca stepped forward, extended her arms in both directions, looking up, saying, &quot;Father Sky, give us rain.&quot;. The sky granted her request instantaneously.<br /> <br /> Being Agnostic, I investigated Wicca as a practice for getting through Arctic Winter, because ritual can ground you and focus the mind. It is significantly more rigorous than clicking on a guided meditation video at the end of a long day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T00:22:57-08:00","id":1496579,"title":"","content":"I always make a point of developing a person's sexuality or gender identity last unless its a plot point. Its partly to avoid pitfalls of writtibg such characters as defined by that. For example my tremere is &quot;ambitious, loyal and anxious.&quot; Rather than &quot;lesbian&quot; which she personally resents due to falling in love with an anarch caitiff.<br /> <br /> I also think some of the games provide interesting potential ideas on what it would mean in that context. For example transgender mages once they hit a certain level of power, can effectively circumvent a lot of the stuff a trans people genrally have to engage with. To the point where I saw a master played by a trans woman just retcon her pre transition life as always been a woman using a lot of time, entropy and mind. Actually led to an interesting ethical discussion where said player commented she wouldn't do the same with that power.<br /> <br /> As always sensitivity is a must.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-09-2022, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T03:41:57-08:00","id":1496582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482713-inventing-lgbt-characters-as-suggestions-for-onyx-writer-team?p=1496565#post1496565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My first serious girlfriend already had a girlfriend, both becoming frequent guests at my mother's place. &amp;quot;We're playing Vampire.&amp;quot;, I would say on our way up the stairs. I have not had any experience of that kind since, didn't pursue such and rarely speak of it, since it was habitual not to in a community whose views were unsupportive of how we felt, their own families included. One was an Atheist with a purely scientific worldview, the other a nominal Christian.<br /> <br /> Completely unconnected and years later, I was at a bus stop with a group of friends on a hot, humid day. A woman who I knew to be a practitioner of Wicca stepped forward, extended her arms in both directions, looking up, saying, &amp;quot;Father Sky, give us rain.&amp;quot;. The sky granted her request instantaneously.<br /> <br /> Being Agnostic, I investigated Wicca as a practice for getting through Arctic Winter, because ritual can ground you and focus the mind. It is significantly more rigorous than clicking on a guided meditation video at the end of a long day.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree with your last paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T03:43:51-08:00","id":1496583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482713-inventing-lgbt-characters-as-suggestions-for-onyx-writer-team?p=1496579#post1496579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always make a point of developing a person's sexuality or gender identity last unless its a plot point. Its partly to avoid pitfalls of writtibg such characters as defined by that. For example my tremere is &quot;ambitious, loyal and anxious.&quot; Rather than &quot;lesbian&quot; which she personally resents due to falling in love with an anarch caitiff.<br /> <br /> I also think some of the games provide interesting potential ideas on what it would mean in that context. For example transgender mages once they hit a certain level of power, can effectively circumvent a lot of the stuff a trans people genrally have to engage with. To the point where I saw a master played by a trans woman just retcon her pre transition life as always been a woman using a lot of time, entropy and mind. Actually led to an interesting ethical discussion where said player commented she wouldn't do the same with that power.<br /> <br /> As always sensitivity is a must.</div> </div> </div> </div>You raise a very good point. Sexuality shouldn\u2019t define a character, but it is a part of them. And yeah, sensitivity is a must. Also, sensitive themes like sexuality are often better dealt with in one on one RP with someone you really trust than in a group context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T19:03:17-08:00","id":1496770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amethyst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482713-inventing-lgbt-characters-as-suggestions-for-onyx-writer-team?p=1496582#post1496582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I totally agree with your last paragraph.</div> </div> </div> </div>To maybe clarify a bit before expanding on our point of total agreement... I don't conflate my the long ago girl-girl-boy experience (which changed me as a person) with girl-girl romances that are <i>exclusive</i>, by default in my imagination. Nor were the separate, individual references in P1 and 2 a denial of lesbian and bisexual Wiccans. I don't know if weather witching is encouraged by the larger Wiccan community or if my friend relied on the weather report to calculate an impressively timed performance. Either way, I was impressed. Onto P3<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <br /> <br /> A practice that involves, athames, altars, candles, herbs, oils and bottles requires space. It requires more space when practitioners gather. I remember doing some searches on both Paganism and Wicca, related to religious buildings and tax exempt status. One Pagan website said that outdoor natural spaces <i>are</i> the temple and that they shun entanglement with large institutions. I also came across content about legal battles to get tax exempt status for Wiccan buildings. <br /> <br /> So, it seems most Wiccans use their primary residence for solo practice and hosting fellow practitioners. Years ago, had there been a Wiccan Temple close to me, I might have explored the religion. Now, I just wonder if there is a gradual way to adopt the simplest practices, given the limited space I have in my primary residence. <br /> <br /> On a side note, a neighbor was trying to give a gift to a woman he likes. She was unsure if she should accept. He said in French that &quot;Le Dieu Cornu&quot; would be upset if she refused, speaking of The Horned God. He was raised Wiccan, but I'm unlikely to seek information from him for other reasons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-10T23:32:35-08:00","id":1496779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1482713-inventing-lgbt-characters-as-suggestions-for-onyx-writer-team?p=1496770#post1496770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To maybe clarify a bit before expanding on our point of total agreement... I don't conflate my the long ago girl-girl-boy experience (which changed me as a person) with girl-girl romances that are <i>exclusive</i>, by default in my imagination. Nor were the separate, individual references in P1 and 2 a denial of lesbian and bisexual Wiccans. I don't know if weather witching is encouraged by the larger Wiccan community or if my friend relied on the weather report to calculate an impressively timed performance. Either way, I was impressed. Onto P3<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. <br /> <br /> A practice that involves, athames, altars, candles, herbs, oils and bottles requires space. It requires more space when practitioners gather. I remember doing some searches on both Paganism and Wicca, related to religious buildings and tax exempt status. One Pagan website said that outdoor natural spaces <i>are</i> the temple and that they shun entanglement with large institutions. I also came across content about legal battles to get tax exempt status for Wiccan buildings. <br /> <br /> So, it seems most Wiccans use their primary residence for solo practice and hosting fellow practitioners. Years ago, had there been a Wiccan Temple close to me, I might have explored the religion. Now, I just wonder if there is a gradual way to adopt the simplest practices, given the limited space I have in my primary residence. <br /> <br /> On a side note, a neighbor was trying to give a gift to a woman he likes. She was unsure if she should accept. He said in French that &amp;quot;Le Dieu Cornu&amp;quot; would be upset if she refused, speaking of The Horned God. He was raised Wiccan, but I'm unlikely to seek information from him for other reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regarding your last paragraph, he shouldn\u2019t have tried to pressure her into accepting the gift. Everything else is totally true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}